course: dictionary
lesson: 7511
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. To pick the right one, read the sentence and look at the clues around the word. «Marsupials, such as kangaroos and koalas, carry their tiny newborns in a pouch.» Marsupials are animals and the newborns are babies, so here a pouch is a pocket of skin on the animal's body.
explain: «Her pencil pouch was full of pens and rubbers.» There is no animal here, and pens are things you carry, so a pouch is a small soft bag. Try the meaning in the sentence: "her small soft bag was full of pens". It still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Sometimes the clue is the body part. «A hamster can stuff its cheeks so full of seeds that its head looks twice as wide» tells you the pouch is inside the cheeks and is for carrying food. Ask yourself: is it a bag, a belly pocket or a cheek pocket? The words around it decide.
fact: A pouch can be a small soft bag, often closed with a string or a zip.
fact: A pouch can also be a pocket of skin on the belly of some animals, where their babies grow.
fact: Some animals, like hamsters, have pouches in their cheeks for carrying food.
fact: Marsupials, such as kangaroos, koalas and wombats, carry their babies, called joeys, in a pouch.
fact: A newborn kangaroo is about the size of a jelly bean, and it crawls into its mother's pouch to drink milk.
exercise: «Mia put her pens in her pencil pouch.» What is a pouch here? | *A small soft bag | A pocket of skin on an animal's belly | A pocket inside a hamster's cheek | A type of wombat
exercise: «The baby kangaroo drank milk in its mother's pouch.» What is a pouch here? | A lunch box | *A pocket of skin on the belly where babies grow | A small soft bag with a zip | A pocket inside a hamster's cheek
exercise: Which animal has pouches in its cheeks for carrying food? | Wombat | Kangaroo | *Hamster | Koala
test: Marsupials carry their tiny newborns in what? | *A pouch | A shell | A nest | A cave
test: Which word means a small soft bag, often closed with a string or zip? | Ladder | Cup | Bowl | *Pouch
exam: «In seahorses the mother puts her eggs into a pouch on the father's belly.» In seahorses, whose belly has the pouch that holds the eggs? | The baby's | The fish's | The mother's | *The father's
